[{"id":"fm-core1-1.20-q1","number":1,"question":"<p>The curve given by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\mathrm f(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)=\\frac{x-3}{x+2}\" data-display=\"true\"></span><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>State the asymptotes of the curve.</p></li><li><p>Sketch <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\mathrm f(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Hence, giving your answer in set notation, find the values when</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{x-3}{x+2}&lt;0\" data-display=\"true\"></span></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=-2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=-\\frac32\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=3\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/1.20/solutions/assets/diagrams/120-p1-1.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\{x:x\\in\\mathbb R,-2&lt;x&lt;3\\}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.20-q2","number":2,"question":"<p>The curve given by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\mathrm f(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)=\\frac{3x+4}{x-1}\" data-display=\"true\"></span><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>State the asymptotes of the curve.</p></li><li><p>Sketch <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\mathrm f(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Hence, giving your answer in interval notation, find the values when</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{3x+4}{x-1}\\ge0\" data-display=\"true\"></span></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=3\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=-4\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=-\\frac43\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/1.20/solutions/assets/diagrams/120-p1-2.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\in(\\infty,-\\frac43]\\cup(-1,\\infty)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.20-q3","number":3,"question":"<p>The curve given by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\mathrm f(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)=\\frac{2x-a}{x-b}\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are positive integers is shown in the diagram below.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/1.20/questions/assets/diagrams/120-q3.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><p>The asymptotes of the curve are given by the equations <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=9\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>State the values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Find the coordinates of where the curve meets the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis.</p></li><li><p>Hence, find the values when</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{2x-a}{x-b}&gt;0\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>Give your answer in set notation.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>Asymptote of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=9\" data-display=\"false\"></span> gives <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b=9\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>Using <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(10,15)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> then <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"15=\\frac{20-a}{10-9}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a=5\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b=9\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\frac59\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=\\frac52\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(\\tfrac52,0)\\text{ and }(0,\\tfrac59)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{2x-5}{x-9}&gt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\{x:x\\in\\mathbb R,x&lt;\\tfrac52\\}\\cup\\{x:x\\in\\mathbb R,x&gt;9\\}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.20-q4","number":4,"question":"<p>The curve given by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\mathrm f(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)=\\frac{1-3x}{4x+5}\" data-display=\"true\"></span><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>State the asymptotes of the curve.</p></li><li><p>Sketch <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\mathrm f(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Hence, find the values when</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{1-3x}{4x+5}&lt;\\frac12\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>Give your answer in set notation.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=-\\frac34\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=-\\frac54\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\frac15\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=\\frac13\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/1.20/solutions/assets/diagrams/120-p3-1.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{1-3x}{4x+5}=\\frac12\\Rightarrow2(1-3x)=4x+5\\Rightarrow-3=10x\\quad\\therefore x=-\\frac3{10}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\{x:x\\in\\mathbb R,x&lt;-\\tfrac54\\}\\cup\\{x:x\\in\\mathbb R,x&gt;-\\tfrac3{10}\\}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.20-q5","number":5,"question":"<p>The curve given by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\mathrm f(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)=\\frac{x}{x^2-k}\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a positive integer is shown in the diagram below.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/1.20/questions/assets/diagrams/120-q5.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><p>The asymptotes of the curve are given by the equations <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=-3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=3\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>State the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>For your value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, solve</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{x}{x^2-k}=\\frac25\" data-display=\"true\"></span></li><li><p>Hence, for your value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> find the values when</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{x}{x^2-k}\\ge\\frac25\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>Give your answer in set notation.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k=9\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{x}{x^2-9}=\\frac25\\Rightarrow5x=2x^2-18\\Rightarrow2x^2-5x-18=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore x=-2\\text{ or }x=\\frac92\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/1.20/solutions/assets/diagrams/120-p4-1.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\{x:x\\in\\mathbb R,-3&lt;x\\le-2\\}\\cup\\{x:x\\in\\mathbb R,3&lt;x\\le\\tfrac92\\}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.20-q6","number":6,"question":"<p>The curve given by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\mathrm f(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)=\\frac{x^2+x-20}{x^2+x-6}\" data-display=\"true\"></span><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>State the asymptotes of the curve.</p></li><li><p>Sketch <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\mathrm f(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Hence, find the values when</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{x^2+x-20}{x^2+x-6}\\le\\frac92\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>Give your answer in interval notation.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x^2+x-6=(x+3)(x-2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>So asymptotes are</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x=-3,\\quad x=2\\text{ and }y=1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=-\\frac{10}3\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x^2+x-20=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=-5\" data-display=\"false\"></span> or <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=4\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/1.20/solutions/assets/diagrams/120-p4-2.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{x^2+x-20}{x^2+x-6}=\\frac92\\Rightarrow2x^2+2x-40=9x^2+9x-54\\Rightarrow7x^2+7x-14=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> or <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=-2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x\\in(-\\infty,3)\\cup[-2,1]\\cup(2,\\infty)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.20-q7","number":7,"question":"<p>A curve is given by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\mathrm f(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)=\\frac{ax^2+4x+b}{x^2-3x+c}\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are integers is shown in the diagram below.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/1.20/questions/assets/diagrams/120-q7.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><p>The asymptote of the curve is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. There is a maximum at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(3,\\frac{16}3)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and a minimum at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-1,0)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Hence, find the values when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)&lt;2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p><p>Give your answer in interval notation.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=\\frac{2x^2+4x+b}{x^2-3x+c}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>At <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-1,0)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"0=2(-1)^2+4(-1)+b\\quad\\therefore b=2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=\\frac{2x^2+4x+2}{x^2-3x+c}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>At <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(3,\\frac{16}3)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{16}3=\\frac{18+12+2}{9-9+c}\\quad\\therefore c=6\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c=6\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{2x^2+4x+2}{x^2-3x+6}=2\\Rightarrow2x^2+4x+2=2x^2-6x+12\\Rightarrow10x=10\\quad\\therefore x=1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x\\in(-\\infty,1)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.20-q8","number":8,"question":"<p>The curve given by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\mathrm f(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)=\\frac{x^2-1}{2x^2-4x+3}\" data-display=\"true\"></span><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>State any asymptotes of the curve.</p></li></ol><p>The line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> intersects the curve.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"2\"><li><p>Show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(2k+1)(k-1)\\le0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Hence find the coordinates of the stationary points of the curve and identify their types.</p></li><li><p>Hence sketch <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\mathrm f(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Find the values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> when</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{x^2-1}{2x^2-4x+3}\\ge x-1\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>Give your answer in set notation.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2x^2-4x+3=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> has no real solutions</p>","<p>So the only asymptote is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\frac12\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\frac{x^2-1}{2x^2-4x+3}=k \\Rightarrow x^2-1=k(2x^2-4x+3)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n \\Rightarrow(1-2k)x^2+4kx-(3k+1)=0\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>There exists solutions when:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n(4k)^2+4(1-2k)(3k+1) \\ge0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n16k^2-24k^2+4k+4 \\ge0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n2k^2-k-1 \\le0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n(2k+1)(k-1) \\le0\\text{ as req.}\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\text{When }y=-\\frac12,\\quad-\\frac12=\\frac{x^2-1}{2x^2-4x+3} \\Rightarrow2x^2-4x+3=2-2x^2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n \\Rightarrow4x^2-4x+1=0\\text{ so }x=\\frac12\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\text{When }y=1,\\quad1=\\frac{x^2-1}{2x^2-4x+3} \\Rightarrow2x^2-4x+3=x^2-1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n \\Rightarrow x^2-4x+4=0\\text{ so }x=2\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Min is at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(\\frac12,-\\frac12)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, Max is at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(2,1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=-\\frac13\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> or <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=-1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/1.20/solutions/assets/diagrams/120-p6-1.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">e)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\frac{x^2-1}{2x^2-4x+3}=x-1 \\Rightarrow x^2-1=(x-1)(2x^2-4x+3)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nx^2-1 =2x^3-4x^2+3x-2x^2+4x-3\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n2x^3-7x^2+7x-2 =0\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Let <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)=2x^3-7x^2+7x-2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\mathrm f(1) =2-7+7-2=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\mathrm f(2) =16-28+14-2=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\mathrm f(\\tfrac12) =\\tfrac14-\\tfrac74+\\tfrac72-2=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\therefore2x^3-7x^2+7x-2 =(x-1)(x-2)(2x-1)=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\therefore x =1,\\quad x=2\\text{ or }x=\\frac12\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\{x:x\\in\\mathbb R,x\\le\\tfrac12\\}\\cup\\{x:x\\in\\mathbb R,1\\le x\\le2\\}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.20-q9","number":9,"question":"<p>It is given that a rational function has equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\mathrm f(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Its graph has exactly two asymptotes <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=-2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p><p>It intersects the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis exactly once at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(3,0)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Hence state the coordinates where the curve meets the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis and the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis.</p></li><li><p>Sketch <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\mathrm f(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Hence, find the value(s) for which <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)\\ge4\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p><p>Give your answer in interval notation.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>Two asymptotes which are perpendicular so of the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\frac{ax+b}{cx+d}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>The asymptotes give: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\frac{-2x+k}{x-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>At <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(3,0)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> then <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0=\\frac{-6+k}{3-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k=6\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)=\\frac{-2x+6}{x-1}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=-6\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=3\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(0,-6)\\text{ and }(3,0)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/1.20/solutions/assets/diagrams/120-p7-1.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{-2x+6}{x-1}=4\\Rightarrow-2x+6=4x-4\\Rightarrow6x=10\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore x=\\frac53\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore x\\in(1,\\tfrac53]\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.20-q10","number":10,"question":"<p>A curve is given by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\mathrm f(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)=\\frac{3x^2+ax+b}{x^2+cx+2}\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are integers.</p><p>It has exactly one asymptote with the equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. The curve passes through the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. The curve has a maximum at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(3,\\frac{29}7)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and a minimum at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-1,-5)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Find the values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where the curve meets the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis.</p></li><li><p>Sketch <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\mathrm f(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Find the value(s) for which <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)\\ge-1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p><p>Give your answer in set notation.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>The curve is of the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\frac{3x^2+ax+b}{x^2+cx+2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>Consider the points:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"-1=\\frac b2\\text{ so }b=-2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>But also</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{29}7=\\frac{3a+25}{3c+11}\\Rightarrow319+87c=21a+175\\Rightarrow21a-87c=144\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"-5=\\frac{1-a}{3-c}\\Rightarrow-15+5c=1-a\\Rightarrow a+5c=16\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a=11\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore\\mathrm f(x)=\\frac{3x^2+11x-2}{x^2+x+2}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3x^2+11x-2=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore x=-\\frac{11}6+\\frac{\\sqrt{145}}6\\text{ or }x=-\\frac{11}6-\\frac{\\sqrt{145}}6\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/1.20/solutions/assets/diagrams/120-p8-1.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n-1=\\frac{3x^2+11x-2}{x^2+x+2} \\Rightarrow-x^2-x-2=3x^2+11x-2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n \\Rightarrow4x^2+12x=0\\Rightarrow4x(x+3)=0\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\therefore x=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> or <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=-3\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\{x:x\\in\\mathbb R,x\\le-3\\}\\cup\\{x:x\\in\\mathbb R,x\\ge0\\}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.20-q11","number":11,"question":"<p>It is given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\mathrm f(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a rational function of quadratic order in both the numerator and denominator of the fraction.</p><p>An incomplete sketch is shown below based on the following information:</p><p>Its graph has exactly three asymptotes which are given by equations <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=-1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=-2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p><p>It crosses the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"1+\\sqrt2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"1-\\sqrt2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and it crosses the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-\\frac14\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/1.20/questions/assets/diagrams/120-q11.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>On a copy of the diagram above, complete the sketch of the curve.</p><p>You should label the asymptotes.</p></li><li><p>Find <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Hence, solve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)\\le-1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p><p>Give your answer in interval notation.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/1.20/solutions/assets/diagrams/120-p9-1.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>Assume the function is of the form: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\frac{ax^2+bx+c}{px^2+qx+r}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(0,-\\frac14)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> gives that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac cr=-\\frac14\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>Numerator: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a(x-(1+\\sqrt2))(x-(1-\\sqrt2))=a(x^2-2x-1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>Denominator: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p(x-2)(x+2)=p(x^2-4)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=-1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> gives that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac ap=-1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore a=-p\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{a(x^2-2x-1)}{-a(x^2-4)}=-\\frac{x^2-2x-1}{x^2-4}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore\\mathrm f(x)=-\\frac{x^2-2x-1}{x^2-4}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"-1=-\\frac{x^2-2x-1}{x^2-4}\\Rightarrow x^2-4=x^2-2x-1\\Rightarrow2x=3\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore x=\\frac32\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore x\\in(-\\infty,-2)\\cup[\\tfrac32,2)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]}]